{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02641",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 6.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Alright, good morning. I've just opened your notes. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.3,
      "end_seconds": 23.34,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a severe sore throat on one side. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.19,
      "end_seconds": 29.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.89,
      "end_seconds": 35.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.46,
      "end_seconds": 41.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.71,
      "end_seconds": 48.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "About a month, I think... sorry, two months, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.48,
      "end_seconds": 56.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "What aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.12,
      "end_seconds": 63.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "It's worse with swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.76,
      "end_seconds": 67.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.21,
      "end_seconds": 72.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Ah, about a seven out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.17,
      "end_seconds": 76.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.93,
      "end_seconds": 98.04,
      "duration_seconds": 21.11,
      "text": "It usually comes with a muffled voice. As for muffled voice, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. About muffled voice, I'd give it a seven, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.91,
      "end_seconds": 118.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "And what about cough, rash or noisy breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.57,
      "end_seconds": 124.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "I haven't had cough, rash or noisy breathing, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.69,
      "end_seconds": 130.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.64,
      "end_seconds": 134.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.13,
      "end_seconds": 137.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.53,
      "end_seconds": 141.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.06,
      "end_seconds": 158.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.2,
      "end_seconds": 171.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. I walk the dog every morning. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.31,
      "end_seconds": 176.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.39,
      "end_seconds": 181.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Erm, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.34,
      "end_seconds": 185.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.22,
      "end_seconds": 193.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Well, yes, I had part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.25,
      "end_seconds": 201.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.55,
      "end_seconds": 205.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I mean, I've had COPD, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.33,
      "end_seconds": 211.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Okay, I can see COPD in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.85,
      "end_seconds": 230.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.66,
      "end_seconds": 240.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.98,
      "end_seconds": 263.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.8,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 104, height 173 centimetres. And blood pressure 108 over 67, SpO2 96 percent on room air, weight 89 kilos, BMI works out to 29.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.38,
      "end_seconds": 268.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.32,
      "end_seconds": 272.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.2,
      "end_seconds": 288.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "The right tonsil is pushed towards the middle, the uvula is deviated, and the palate is swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.67,
      "end_seconds": 306.08,
      "duration_seconds": 15.41,
      "text": "Okay, thank you, you can get dressed. Let me tell you where I've got to. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a quinsy, a peritonsillar abscess or severe tonsillitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.06,
      "end_seconds": 314.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.06,
      "end_seconds": 352.55,
      "duration_seconds": 36.49,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a quinsy, a peritonsillar abscess, and we'll know more once the an urgent ENT drainage is back. I want an urgent ENT drainage done, that's for peritonsillar abscess. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. You'll be taking benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, now, single dose. That's for peritonsillar abscess. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.21,
      "end_seconds": 354.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.74,
      "end_seconds": 378.16,
      "duration_seconds": 21.42,
      "text": "You need to be seen by ENT today to drain it. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll also refer you to the ENT team. Book a review straight away. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.08,
      "end_seconds": 382.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.61,
      "end_seconds": 385.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}